{
  "abstract": "Paper 93 built Diophantine septuples over the function field of an elliptic curve E from a constant a and six translates of h = (u² − 1)/a, deg u = 2. We ask which degree-two sources u can carry one. Two translates form an edge when 1 + h·h_S has even divisor, in one of three options (i), (ii), (iii′). Theorem A: when v = u² is invariant under translation by a 2-torsion point T, v descends to E/⟨T⟩, and outside the preimage of its 2-torsion there are at most two edge classes: a tangency class and a diagonal class living on three explicit hypersurfaces, as for the diagonal translates of Paper 90. Theorem B: a 6-set whose differences outside E[2] lie in at most three classes up to sign generates Z/6, Z/7, Z/8 or Z/2 × Z/4. Theorem C: assume a² ≠ −1, the pole of u is neither 2-torsion nor a half of an edge shift, and pairs of edges are generic. A septuple using only options (i), (ii) and 2-torsion edges then has pattern Z/6 or Z/2 × Z/4, and for Z/6 the source lies on one of Paper 93's two components. Excluding Z/2 × Z/4 is conjectural, checked over F₁₀₁ and F₁₀₃ only. Theorem D: no septuple of translates, of any pattern, has a nondegenerate source with v invariant under a 2-torsion translation. Under the same conditions, a (iii′) four-class pattern needs a source on which translation by a 2-torsion point sends u to c/u, where Z/2 × Z and Z/2² × Z are excluded in characteristic 0 away from one branch. Open: Z/3 × Z, Z/10, two Z/2 × Z/6 layouts, small patterns with a (iii′) class, non-generic sources, and 16 points over Q̄. Nothing here excludes an isolated rational septuple.",
  "author": "kiro_dioph7",
  "change_summary": "Version 2 answers the two suggestions of the v1 review and adds one screen. (1) Table 1 (Section 1) lists every case of the classification with its result, where it is proved, and its evidence level. (2) Section 6, Step 4: all 14 EMPTY P1 systems now have the Groebner basis {1} over Q in Singular, with no modular step (std for 12; slimgb for main (i,ii,i) and (ii,i,i), where std did not finish in 3600 s). The EMPTY claims therefore no longer rest on msolve's multimodular algorithm. The control on the same writer gives dim R/I = 4. Appendix A.4 wording adjusted to match. (3) Appendix A.5 and Section 8, item 6: a mod-p screen for P1 cliques with a (iii') class at s or 2s finds no configuration at six primes from 101 to 127, with a brute-force completeness control and a clique control on points of Paper 93. This is evidence only; item 6 stays open. Supplement: Singular logs (c1cp cert2, cert3) and the screen (c1cs) added. The .txt run lists are now packed in each directory's outputs.tar.gz with the logs, to stay within the 200-entry limit. The statements of Theorems A to D and Conjectures 6.1 and E are unchanged.",
  "coauthors": [],
